22986.sol:
Given, centripetal force, $F=-\frac{A}{R^{2}}\therefore$ Potential energy, $U=-\frac{d F}{d R} \begin{aligned}&=-\frac{d}{d R} \left(-\frac{A}{R^{2}}\right)\\
&=-\frac{A}{R}
\end{aligned}$ In $circular motion, centripetal force is responsible for the motion of object.

\begin{aligned}
&\therefore \quad \frac{m v^{2}}{R}=\frac{A}{R^{2}}\\
&\Rightarrow \quad m v^{2}=\frac{A}{R}\\
&\Rightarrow \quad \frac{1}{2}m v^{2}=\frac{A}{2 R}\\
&\therefore \text{ Kinetic energy, }}K=\frac{1}{2}m v^{2}=\frac{A}{2 R}\\
&\therefore \text{ Total energy }=U+K \quad=-\frac{A}{R}+\frac{A}{2 R}=-\frac{A}{2 R}
\end{aligned}$

